00:27:45.980 --> 00:27:46.980
This is one of them.

00:27:46.980 --> 00:27:48.980
So I suggest you back off.

00:27:48.980 --> 00:27:50.980
Sorry, but backing off?

00:27:50.980 --> 00:27:52.980
Not exactly my strongest suit.

00:27:52.980 --> 00:27:54.980
Where's Oliver?

00:27:56.980 --> 00:28:23.339
I prefer to make my own luck.

00:28:23.339 --> 00:29:12.400
Your luck hasn't run out.

00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:32.099
I'm disappointed, Oliver.

00:29:32.099 --> 00:29:36.099
You lack the killer instinct after all.

00:29:36.099 --> 00:29:50.099
Toss the gun.

00:29:50.099 --> 00:29:51.099
You know, true gamesman?

00:29:51.099 --> 00:29:53.099
You know, cheat by stacking the deck.

00:29:53.099 --> 00:29:54.099
in the deck.

00:29:54.099 --> 00:30:01.660
Well, everything was aces until your girlfriend showed up.

00:30:01.660 --> 00:30:03.660
As always, I had to play the hand I was dealt.

00:30:03.660 --> 00:30:05.660
So don't she just let her go.

00:30:05.660 --> 00:30:06.660
You didn't play by my rules.

00:30:06.660 --> 00:30:07.660
Why should I play by yours?

00:30:07.660 --> 00:30:09.660
You were supposed to shoot her.

00:30:09.660 --> 00:30:11.660
See, that's what I don't understand.

00:30:11.660 --> 00:30:13.660
You could have killed her yourself.

00:30:13.660 --> 00:30:15.660
You could have shot me when I walked through the door.

00:30:15.660 --> 00:30:17.660
Why set the scene?

00:30:17.660 --> 00:30:19.660
When can tie up loose ends with a simple square knot?

00:30:19.660 --> 00:30:23.660
Or one can choose some more elegant clove relief.

00:30:23.660 --> 00:30:24.660
It's all a matter of style.

00:30:24.660 --> 00:30:26.660
It's all a matter of style.

00:30:26.660 --> 00:30:29.660
Oh, and I'd say I'm sorry for taking your money,

00:30:29.660 --> 00:30:32.660
except in your case it hardly matters.

00:30:32.660 --> 00:30:34.660
I can't take it with you.

00:30:34.660 --> 00:30:41.140
I know this isn't just part of your game.

00:30:41.140 --> 00:30:44.119
Right.

00:30:44.119 --> 00:31:03.180
She knows I won't, not if there's a chance I'd hit you.

00:31:03.180 --> 00:31:04.180
Gasoline.

00:31:04.180 --> 00:31:07.180
I thought I'd torch the place and we're done.

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:09.180
Clover not.

00:31:09.180 --> 00:31:10.180
No.

00:31:10.180 --> 00:31:12.180
I just like playing with fire.

00:31:12.180 --> 00:31:20.460
Never bet against the house.

00:31:20.460 --> 00:31:55.859
Lois!

00:31:55.859 --> 00:31:56.859
Come on.

00:31:56.859 --> 00:31:59.859
Why did you come?

00:31:59.859 --> 00:32:01.859
You could have left me here.

00:32:01.859 --> 00:32:03.859
After everything I put you through, no one would blame you.

00:32:03.859 --> 00:32:05.859
I'm gonna blame myself.

00:32:05.859 --> 00:32:07.859
Listen, I don't care what you're doing.

00:32:07.859 --> 00:32:09.859
Or who you are, I'm gonna get you the hell out of here.

00:32:09.859 --> 00:32:11.859
All right? I'll go let you die.

00:32:11.859 --> 00:32:13.859
Come on.

00:32:13.859 --> 00:32:34.849
What the hell is this?

00:32:34.849 --> 00:32:38.849
You kept asking me who did this to you?

00:32:38.849 --> 00:32:41.849
My question was always the answer.

00:32:41.849 --> 00:32:43.849
Who did you destroy?

00:32:43.849 --> 00:33:05.230
I hear you're someone.

00:33:05.230 --> 00:33:11.640
sort of hero, one that tried to bury that part of himself.

00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:14.640
You've just proven that hero is still alive, Oliver.

00:33:14.640 --> 00:33:18.269
Now it's time to resurrect.

00:33:18.269 --> 00:33:38.029
Nicely played.

00:33:38.029 --> 00:33:47.559
I started asking myself who knew about Lex,

00:33:47.559 --> 00:33:52.559
about Toy Man, the things I'd given up, what I tried to do.

00:33:52.559 --> 00:33:55.559
And it all occurred to me.

00:33:55.559 --> 00:33:58.559
Dinah shattered the glass in the warehouse,

00:33:58.559 --> 00:34:00.559
bar rescue me from the car, Victor faked the computers,

00:34:00.559 --> 00:34:01.559
and watchtower kept an eye on the whole thing.

00:34:01.559 --> 00:34:03.559
deny on the whole thing, right?

00:34:03.559 --> 00:34:12.809
You were living like you had a death wish, Oliver.

00:34:12.809 --> 00:34:15.809
You had to face your demons if you were ever going to make it out alive,

00:34:15.809 --> 00:34:20.860
and I had to push you over the ledge in order to pull you back.

00:34:20.860 --> 00:34:22.860
Did you have to push with a three-ton truck?

00:34:22.860 --> 00:34:25.860
I didn't think a tricycle would be a strong enough point.

00:34:25.860 --> 00:34:28.860
You're a fighter, Oliver.

00:34:28.860 --> 00:34:30.860
You fought for yourself and for a second change.

00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:37.019
Chloe, I'm not the only one you put at risk.

00:34:37.019 --> 00:34:40.019
If you're worried about our little club and Lex, don't be.

00:34:40.019 --> 00:34:42.019
I played my cards close to my chest.

00:34:42.019 --> 00:34:43.019
chest.

00:34:43.019 --> 00:34:44.019
And Lois was what?

00:34:44.019 --> 00:34:46.019
She was just another ace up your sleep?

00:34:46.019 --> 00:34:48.019
No, I never meant for her to get involved.

00:34:48.019 --> 00:34:52.019
She was chasing after you when she accidentally ended up storming the fields.

00:34:52.019 --> 00:34:54.019
That's when Victoria went off script.

00:34:54.019 --> 00:34:56.019
I could have killed her.

00:34:56.019 --> 00:35:01.019
No offense to your manhood, but I made sure that your gun was loaded with blanks just in case.

00:35:01.019 --> 00:35:05.019
I trust you, Oliver, just not that much.

00:35:05.019 --> 00:35:11.909
Did Clark know about this?

00:35:11.909 --> 00:35:14.909
You can't be serious.

00:35:14.909 --> 00:35:16.909
Clark would never in a million years,

00:35:16.909 --> 00:35:21.309
risk what needed to be done.

00:35:21.309 --> 00:35:23.309
Well, he's led a different life than we have, hasn't.

00:35:23.309 --> 00:35:29.250
I can't expect him to know me like you do.

00:35:29.250 --> 00:35:35.250
The places that I'd sunk to, the depths you must have had to go to bring me back.

00:35:35.250 --> 00:35:43.650
You proved it to yourself.

00:35:43.650 --> 00:35:48.650
Even with your face and the better, you still had the hero in your heart.

00:35:48.650 --> 00:35:57.300
You saved my life, Chloe.

00:35:57.300 --> 00:36:00.300
Both the myth and the man.

00:36:00.300 --> 00:36:21.480
So, what was that about?

00:36:21.480 --> 00:36:23.480
Uh-oh, I've seen that look before.

00:36:23.480 --> 00:36:27.480
that look before, usually right before you sock me in the jaw.

00:36:27.480 --> 00:36:28.480
Tempted.

00:36:28.480 --> 00:36:30.480
But if you're unconscious, you can't answer any questions,

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:33.480
like who the hell was that dragon lady?

00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:34.480
Okay.

00:36:34.480 --> 00:36:39.480
She was, um, a psycho ex-girlfriend who watched fatal attraction too many times.

00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:41.480
So what am I, the bunny?

00:36:41.480 --> 00:36:43.480
Oliver.

00:36:43.480 --> 00:36:46.480
You really need to take a dip in the sane chick pool.

00:36:46.480 --> 00:36:48.480
I mean that dress?

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:50.480
There's a bigger red scare than Cold War Russia.

00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:54.139
Although I thought you wore it pretty well.

00:36:54.139 --> 00:37:01.300
well.

00:37:01.300 --> 00:37:10.820
But, um, you never should have been dragged into this mess I made in my life, and, uh, I'm sorry.

00:37:10.820 --> 00:37:22.059
Was the mess so bad that cleaning it up seemed harder than throwing it all away?

00:37:23.889 --> 00:37:25.889
I saw the video.

00:37:25.889 --> 00:37:27.889
That's enough to send anyone on a binge.

00:37:27.889 --> 00:37:36.000
Did you come talk to me?

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:50.139
Pride, fear, and, um, regret.

00:37:50.139 --> 00:37:53.139
Close to the truth is I've been fighting my demons for so long.

00:37:53.139 --> 00:37:55.139
It just wanted this war to end.

00:37:55.139 --> 00:37:57.139
I wanted this war to end.

00:37:57.139 --> 00:38:05.599
And you felt like there was nothing in life worth fighting for.

00:38:05.599 --> 00:38:10.420
I never felt that way when I was with you.

00:38:10.420 --> 00:38:12.420
I mean, uh...

00:38:12.420 --> 00:38:21.010
I just, I think what I mean is I, uh, I lost sight of what was good in my life.

00:38:21.010 --> 00:38:28.619
I know things between you and me have changed, right?

00:38:28.619 --> 00:38:32.440
Some things haven't changed.

00:38:32.440 --> 00:38:39.019
Oli, I will always be here for you.

00:38:39.019 --> 00:38:49.260
And if you forget that again, I will knock you out.

00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:59.230
Now, I believe there is a certain birthday tradition we have to uphold.

00:38:59.230 --> 00:39:02.280
Hmm.

00:39:02.280 --> 00:39:03.280
Ah.

00:39:03.280 --> 00:39:04.280
Ready to get your asking?

00:39:04.280 --> 00:39:06.280
Hey, I'm ready.

00:39:06.280 --> 00:39:22.269
You've got to stop giving out keys.

00:39:22.269 --> 00:39:26.269
I take it sure all knew something about the alien assassin?

00:39:26.269 --> 00:39:27.269
He recognized her.

00:39:27.269 --> 00:39:31.269
Turns out the symbol tattooed on her shoulder is her family crest.

00:39:31.269 --> 00:39:34.269
Her name's Aaliyah. She's Kandorian.

00:39:34.269 --> 00:39:37.269
I thought Kandor exploded with the rest of Krypton.

00:39:37.269 --> 00:39:39.269
So did I.

00:39:39.269 --> 00:39:41.269
But Jerelle said if she say there may be others.

00:39:41.269 --> 00:39:45.269
And they'll have each left, a kryptonian symbol marking their rival.

00:39:45.269 --> 00:39:47.269
We better start looking.

00:39:47.269 --> 00:39:52.269
We can use watchtower to run a search algorithm that would cross-reference

00:39:52.269 --> 00:39:55.269
all the satellite images with my cryptonian lexicon.

00:39:55.269 --> 00:39:58.269
In other news, Oliver's back.

00:39:58.269 --> 00:40:03.679
Seems like more than just the cooling off. What happened?

00:40:03.679 --> 00:40:05.679
Maybe the scam artist really did a number on him.

00:40:05.679 --> 00:40:09.219
Or you just needed to get some perspective.

00:40:09.219 --> 00:40:14.800
I've found one.

00:40:22.860 --> 00:40:24.860
We definitely didn't come alone.

00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:58.989
I heard you were back.

00:40:58.989 --> 00:41:00.989
You do know, of course, you look absolutely ridiculous in that, right?

00:41:00.989 --> 00:41:08.639
And I got a great tailor, hook you up with a little color, maybe.

00:41:08.639 --> 00:41:11.639
Nice to see you finally discovered something with living for, after all.

00:41:11.639 --> 00:41:13.639
Yeah, I'm like a rediscovery, actually.

00:41:13.639 --> 00:41:18.619
You've done a hell of a job keeping the world safe on your own, Clark.

00:41:18.619 --> 00:41:22.159
I'm here to help you now.

00:41:22.159 --> 00:41:26.590
Good.

00:41:26.590 --> 00:41:27.590
Something tells me.

00:41:27.590 --> 00:41:30.590
Soon the world will need all the help we can get.

